s></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIZUNUMA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAEGUSA KAZUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAKI AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IGUCHI, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUNUMA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAEGUSA, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAKI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A vinyl chloride resin composition with excellent weatherability and impact strength which comprises (a) a vinyl chloride resin, (b) a graft copolymer which is obtained by grafting a monomer ingredient (b2) comprising 40 to 100 wt.% methyl methacrylate and 0 to 60 wt.% at least one member selected from the group consisting of alkyl acrylates, alkyl methacrylates, unsaturated nitriles, and aromatic vinyl compounds onto a crosslinked rubber polymer (b1) obtained mainly from an alkyl acrylate and in which the components soluble in methyl ethyl ketone have an  eta sp/c of 1 to 5 as measured on 0.2g/100 cc acetone solution at 30 DEG C, and (c) calcium carbonate; and a multilayered molded article having a layer formed from the composition as a surface layer or inner layer.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne, d'une part une composition de résine de chlorure de vinyl présentant une bonne résistance aux intempéries et aux chocs, et d'autre part un article moulé multicouche dont une couche de surface ou intérieure est faite dans cette composition. Cette composition comprend (a) une résine de chlorure de vinyl, (b) un copolymère greffe, et (c) du carbonate de calcium. Ce copolymère greffe (b) résulte d'une greffe d'un ingrédient monomère (b2) sur un polymère de gomme réticulée (b1). Ce dernier (b1) provient essentiellement d'un alkylacrylate dans lequel les composants solubles dans le méthyl-éthylcétone présentent un  eta sp/c de 1 à 5 mesuré sur une solution acétonique à 0,2g/100cc à 30 DEG C. L'ingrédient monomère (b2) comprend pour 40% à 100% de sa masse du méthyl-méthacrylate, et pour 0% à 60% de sa masse l'un au moins des éléments du groupe des alkyl-acrylates, alkyl-méthacrylates, nitriles insaturés, et composés aromatiques du vinyl.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>